  "notes": "Modified cash basis school district; all funds incl. School Nutrition are governmental, no business-type funds. Receipts/disbursements from Total Governmental Funds column (p4-5); beginning/ending cash = total fund balances (cash, CDs, investment pool, county treasurer). Balance sheet from the government-wide net position section (p3). Detail uses the budget-and-actual schedules by fund (pp10-16); the General Fund components combining schedule (pp7-8) and nonmajor combining schedule (p9) duplicate them and were not re-entered. Depreciation Fund is combined into General Fund on the statement (GF 2,981,255 = 2,971,661 + 9,594). General Fund transfer 107,109 = Activities 70,000 + School Nutrition 37,109, recorded as other financing in detail. Budget-only lines with blank 2025 actuals (4530, 4525, 3160, 3551, nonrevenue receipts, special building capital improvements, school nutrition capital outlay) omitted. Public power district sales tax and nameplate tax categorized as other taxes. Reclassification column on p8 moves state categorical 11,579 and federal programs 73,223 into regular and special ed instruction (not transfers). Read pages 1-16 of 16 Support services - pupils 376,232 split by fund column (p4, p9): General Fund 182,616 support services; Activity Fund 193,616 student activities."
